description:
Exploration question: Where is `retryDelay` defined, and what calls it? Give every location.

Files read (every line is numbered as `line | code`; this is everything that has been read):

`src/net/retry.ts`
```
1 | import { clamp } from "../util/math";
2 | 
3 | export interface RetryOptions {
4 |   baseMs: number;
5 |   maxMs: number;
6 | }
7 | 
8 | export function retryDelay(attempt: number, opts: RetryOptions): number {
9 |   const raw = opts.baseMs * 2 ** attempt;
10 |   return clamp(raw, 0, opts.maxMs);
11 | }
12 | 
13 | export function shouldRetry(status: number): boolean {
14 |   return status === 429 || status >= 500;
15 | }
```

